# ⛔ Every text file is checked out with LF line ends, on every host.
#
# Git for Windows converts LF to CRLF on checkout by default. A shell script, a
# Dockerfile or an asset copied into a Linux container then carries a carriage
# return on every line and fails there, and every file hashed into an image tag
# or a record hashes to other bytes than on Linux. `text=auto` leaves binary
# files alone.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Kept byte for byte as their authors ship them.
src/studyforge/render/assets/*.LICENSE -text
*.woff2 binary
